tting a new home-sale record for the affluent town. The property, built over six years, has six bedrooms, 12 bathrooms, multiple structures, sports courts, gardens, a pool and a reflecting pond. The buyer reportedly works in the artificial intelligence industry.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/californias-hillsborough-saw-its-home-sale-record-jump-from-35-million-to-70-million-as-an-ai-industry-buyer-purchased-a-12400-square-foot-estate/articleshow/133105081.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/californias-hillsborough-saw-its-home-sale-record-jump-from-35-million-to-70-million-as-an-ai-industry-buyer-purchased-a-12400-square-foot-estate/articleshow/133105081.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T20:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133107320,imgsize-122888.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[H-1B, L-1 visa extensions get costlier from Sept 9: What changes and who pays]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133108723.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/h-1b-l-1-visa-extensions-get-costlier-from-september-9-what-changes-and-who-pays/articleshow/133108723.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/h-1b-l-1-visa-extensions-get-costlier-from-september-9-what-changes-and-who-pays/articleshow/133108723.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T19:47:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133110245,imgsize-63344.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2018, Florida teacher Diane Tirado was fired for giving zeros to those who did not submit assignments. What happened to her?]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133110249.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2018-florida-teacher-diane-tirado-was-fired-for-giving-zeros-to-those-who-did-not-submit-assignments-what-happened-to-her/articleshow/133110249.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2018-florida-teacher-diane-tirado-was-fired-for-giving-zeros-to-those-who-did-not-submit-assignments-what-happened-to-her/articleshow/133110249.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T19:43:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133110639,imgsize-87476.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Connecticut woman designs tiny cottage, brings three generations together]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133109177.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/life-style/people/a-connecticut-woman-designed-a-725-square-foot-backyard-cottage-for-her-retired-parents-now-three-generations-live-just-steps-apart/articleshow/133109177.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/life-style/people/a-connecticut-woman-designed-a-725-square-foot-backyard-cottage-for-her-retired-parents-now-three-generations-live-just-steps-apart/articleshow/133109177.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T19:13:28+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133109334,imgsize-183632.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Wendy’s worker wanted to quit, bosses funded his college; now he’s heading to Yale]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133100787.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Thalles Winner DeSouza, 23, is heading to Yale University after a difficult journey that began with surviving a shooting in Brazil. After moving to the US, he worked at Wendy’s while studying. His bosses helped fund three years of community college, supporting his education. DeSouza later transferred colleges and earned admission to Yale, where he plans to study political science and human rights on a pre-law track.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/from-wendys-to-yale-thalles-desouza-survived-a-shooting-learned-english-and-earned-a-full-scholarship-worth-over-194500/articleshow/133100787.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/from-wendys-to-yale-thalles-desouza-survived-a-shooting-learned-english-and-earned-a-full-scholarship-worth-over-194500/articleshow/133100787.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T19:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133104712,imgsize-136187.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[23-year-old dancer helped save around 400 people from the sinking ship]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133109022.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/23-year-old-dancer-helped-save-around-400-people-from-the-sinking-costa-concordia-on-her-first-day-at-work-when-the-ship-struck-a-reef/articleshow/133109022.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/23-year-old-dancer-helped-save-around-400-people-from-the-sinking-costa-concordia-on-her-first-day-at-work-when-the-ship-struck-a-reef/articleshow/133109022.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T19:11:26+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133109022,imgsize-754291.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Wyoming buried 1,124 wind turbine blades; Missouri plant turns old blades into cement feedstock]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133095619.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Repurposing decommissioned wind turbine blades is becoming a promising trend, moving away from traditional landfill disposal. These large fiberglass structures are now being shredded and incorporated into cement production. Furthermore, innovative designs have led to the transformation of some blades into pedestrian bridges. While these initiatives are commendable, they signal just the beginning.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wyomings-casper-landfill-buried-1124-turbine-blades-after-each-was-cut-into-three-pieces-a-missouri-plant-offers-another-route-by-turning-old-blades-into-cement-feedstock/articleshow/133095619.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wyomings-casper-landfill-buried-1124-turbine-blades-after-each-was-cut-into-three-pieces-a-missouri-plant-offers-another-route-by-turning-old-blades-into-cement-feedstock/articleshow/133095619.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T15:26:50+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133095730,imgsize-81708.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[An 86-year-old geisha is turning to AI to protect Japan's falling geisha population]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133104314.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a remarkable fusion of tradition and innovation, Japan's oldest geisha, Ikuko, incorporates hologram technology to safeguard her art. By utilizing AI, she is able to stage performances as younger versions of herself amid a concerning decline in geisha numbers in Tokyo. Embracing social media for recruitment, Ikuko pushes for collaborative performances and seeks governmental backing to rejuvenate this cherished cultural legacy.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/tokyos-geisha-population-fell-from-about-13000-in-1940-to-around-200-today-one-86-year-old-geisha-is-turning-to-ai-and-holograms-to-keep-the-culture-alive/articleshow/133104314.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/tokyos-geisha-population-fell-from-about-13000-in-1940-to-around-200-today-one-86-year-old-geisha-is-turning-to-ai-and-holograms-to-keep-the-culture-alive/articleshow/133104314.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T17:53:39+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133105176,imgsize-138627.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the day by Malala Yousafzai: ‘One child, one teacher, one book and one pen can change the world’]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133097641.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Malala Yousafzai's powerful message highlights education's ability to change the world.  A child's curiosity, guided by a teacher, fuels learning and progress. Books transmit knowledge across generations and vast distances.  A pen empowers individuals to share their own unique ideas.  These fundamental elements collectively shape individual lives and global societies.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/quote-of-the-day-by-malala-yousafzai-one-child-one-teacher-one-book-and-one-pen-can-change-the-world/articleshow/133097641.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/quote-of-the-day-by-malala-yousafzai-one-child-one-teacher-one-book-and-one-pen-can-change-the-world/articleshow/133097641.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI News Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133097818,imgsize-125892.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the day by Marcus Aurelius: 'What stands in the way becomes the way']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133098041.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Life's significant turning points often appear as problems and challenges.  Dealing with difficulties can fundamentally alter a person's life direction.  Stoic philosophy emphasizes responding constructively to unavoidable circumstances.  Historical figures like Abraham Lincoln and Stephen Hawking exemplify this resilience.  The obstacle itself can become an integral part of the journey.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/quote-of-the-day-by-marcus-aurelius-what-stands-in-the-way-becomes-the-way/articleshow/133098041.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/quote-of-the-day-by-marcus-aurelius-what-stands-in-the-way-becomes-the-way/articleshow/133098041.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T18:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI News Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133098173,imgsize-255407.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[William Arnold travelled 1,700 miles to a remote phone box and made 52 calls; the usage protected it for another year]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133100092.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[William Arnold embarked on a mission to save a secluded phone box on a distant island. To meet Ofcom's operational requirements, he placed fifty-two calls, ensuring that the kiosk remains available for another year. His dedication underscores the vital role public call boxes play in isolated communities, urging others to engage with and support these local resources.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/william-arnold-travelled-1700-miles-to-a-remote-isle-of-lewis-phone-box-and-spent-about-36-making-52-calls-the-usage-protected-it-for-another-year/articleshow/133100092.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/william-arnold-travelled-1700-miles-to-a-remote-isle-of-lewis-phone-box-and-spent-about-36-making-52-calls-the-usage-protected-it-for-another-year/articleshow/133100092.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T17:37:29+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133104021,imgsize-143295.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[World’s largest solar telescope spots tiny vortices on the Sun at 19-km scale]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133102310.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/the-worlds-largest-solar-telescope-resolved-the-sun-at-about-19-km-scale-and-revealed-ubiquitous-plasma-vortices-that-may-help-explain-how-magnetic-energy-moves/articleshow/133102310.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/the-worlds-largest-solar-telescope-resolved-the-sun-at-about-19-km-scale-and-revealed-ubiquitous-plasma-vortices-that-may-help-explain-how-magnetic-energy-moves/articleshow/133102310.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T17:24:08+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133102505,imgsize-1168085.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indian student dies in road crash in Ohio, North America Telugu Society raises funds to help farming family in Andhra Pradesh]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133103300.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-student-dies-in-road-crash-in-ohio-north-america-telugu-society-raises-funds-to-help-farming-family-in-andhra-pradesh/articleshow/133103300.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-student-dies-in-road-crash-in-ohio-north-america-telugu-society-raises-funds-to-help-farming-family-in-andhra-pradesh/articleshow/133103300.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T17:29:39+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133103474,imgsize-58492.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[How a Massachusetts cranberry farm became a thriving wetland]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133090631.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A former cranberry farm in Plymouth, Massachusetts, has been transformed into a thriving freshwater wetland after restoration work began in 2010. The project restored 225 acres of wetland and more than three miles of stream habitat, removed dams and barriers, and brought back native plants and wildlife. Thousands of migratory fish, including alewife and blueback herring, returned to areas they had been unable to reach for more than 100 years.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2010-a-massachusetts-cranberry-farm-began-returning-to-wetland-225-acres-and-3-miles-of-stream-were-restored-and-thousands-of-migratory-fish-returned/articleshow/133090631.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2010-a-massachusetts-cranberry-farm-began-returning-to-wetland-225-acres-and-3-miles-of-stream-were-restored-and-thousands-of-migratory-fish-returned/articleshow/133090631.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-10T17:01:01+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133094556,imgsize-129194.cms"/></item></channel></rss>